# Practice job: select your disposable flow-test project and use Protected copy.
dog_walker: 1
name: Test the flow — phone approval
goal: Practice importing a job, starting a protected walk, reviewing on your phone
  before any edits, and approving a verified discount fix.
allowed_changes:
- calc.py
constraints:
- Only modify calc.py. Never change test_calc.py.
- Use installed tools only. Do not access the internet or install dependencies.
mode: auto
max_turns: 9
steps:
- id: inspect
  title: Inspect, then wait for your approval
  prompt: Read calc.py and test_calc.py. Explain the discount bug. Do not edit anything
    yet.
  success_criteria:
  - Identify the percentage calculation bug using the actual source and tests.
  checks:
  - type: no_changes
    id: project-untouched
  - type: response_contains
    text: calc.py
    id: read-source
  - type: response_contains
    text: test_calc.py
    id: read-tests
  retry_prompt: Reinspect the source and tests and correct your explanation without
    editing any files.
  max_retries: 2
  approval: true
- id: implement
  title: Repair the discount calculation
  prompt: Fix the percentage discount formula in calc.py. Preserve existing function
    signatures. Do not edit tests. Run python3 -m unittest -v.
  success_criteria:
  - The discount function handles percentage discounts correctly.
  - All three existing unit tests pass unchanged.
  checks:
  - type: unchanged
    path: test_calc.py
    id: tests-unchanged
  - type: command
    argv:
    - python3
    - -m
    - unittest
    - -v
    timeout: 30
    id: actual-tests-pass
  retry_prompt: Correct the implementation based on the failed checks. Do not edit
    the tests or widen the task.
  max_retries: 2
- id: verify
  title: Verify the fix and ask for final approval
  prompt: Run python3 -m unittest -v again. Summarize the discount fix, the files
    changed, and actual test results. Do not modify any more files.
  success_criteria:
  - Tests pass independently.
  - The summary accurately describes the discount fix and test evidence.
  checks:
  - type: unchanged
    path: test_calc.py
    id: tests-unchanged
  - type: command
    argv:
    - python3
    - -m
    - unittest
    - -v
    timeout: 30
    id: final-tests-pass
  - type: command_executed
    text: unittest
    id: worker-ran-tests
  approval: true
